%% Title: State · processing job lifecycle
%% Summary: The statuses a processing_jobs row moves through, for scheduled collection cycles and for single jobs (refresh, standup, manual, demo), and when bias checks run.
%% Sources: src/collectors/cycle.js (currentCycleJob, claimDueCycles, closeCycles), src/collectors/runner.js (scoreVia, touch), src/collectors/stale-jobs.js (sweepStaleJobs), src/workers/maintenance.worker.js, src/routes/refresh.js, src/workers/{collect,ingest}.worker.js, scripts/populate.js, src/db/migrations/001, 019, 021, 040. Spec: TECHNICAL_SPEC.md sections 7 (POST /api/refresh), 9 (when bias checks run) and 19 (Tier 3); PR #22 decision G4.
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR

  state "running" as running
  state "closing" as closing
  state "awaiting_retries" as awaiting
  state "completed" as completed
  state "failed" as failed

  [*] --> running : cron cycle created at the first new post of a window (triggered_by cron)
  [*] --> running : refresh (api), standup, manual or demo job created

  running --> closing : cron only, window + 60 s grace over and inflight_runs 0, or hard cap reached
  closing --> completed : posts counted from decision_audit_log, bias checks once when posts exist
  closing --> failed : close error (scrubbed)
  closing --> closing : cron only, re-claimed when its closer died (still closing 2 x the hard cap after started_at)

  running --> completed : single job run finished with no reserved scoring slot held, posts counted from decision_audit_log, bias checks when any
  running --> awaiting : single job still holding reserved scoring slots (a refresh's queued ingest jobs, or scoring retries)
  awaiting --> closing : retries done (inflight_runs 0) or hard cap reached
  running --> failed : single job only — run threw (a cron cycle stays running), enqueue failed (refresh 503), or no progress (last_progress_at, else started_at) for REFRESH_STALE_MINUTES (api) or STALE_JOB_MINUTES (30), marked by the refresh route or the stale-job sweeper (maintenance job, every 5 min)

  completed --> [*]
  failed --> [*]

  note right of running
    one running api job at a time:
    partial unique index uq_processing_jobs_api_running
    (migration 019)
  end note

  note right of completed
    rows are never removed (spec section 19 Tier 3, G4).
    legend: all done (every element is on master)
  end note

  classDef done fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,color:#1b3d1f
  class running, closing, awaiting, completed, failed done
